+A supervisor stops the old gateway with `SIGTERM`, which drains: new work is
+refused and a pending approval can no longer be answered. To have `SIGTERM`
+restart gracefully instead, as `SIGUSR1` does, set:
+
+```yaml title="~/.hermes/config.yaml"
+gateway:
+  sigterm_restart_wait: true
+agent:
+  restart_after_turn_timeout: 540
+```
+
+Active turns then finish within `agent.restart_after_turn_timeout`, clients can
+still answer approvals and clarify questions, and new input is committed for
+the next gateway. A second `SIGTERM` stops at once. Keep the restart wait plus
+`agent.restart_drain_timeout` and a minute of shutdown below the supervisor's
+stop budget. New connections are refused during the wait, except the socket
+tickets and reads a client needs to answer a parked prompt; list plugins in
+`gateway.restart_wait_plugin_sockets` (for example `[device]`) whose WebSocket
+routes the finishing turns depend on, so those connections can come back.
+Before it exits, a stopping gateway releases its idle cached agents, and a memory
+provider's shutdown can take up to its HTTP timeout per agent (30 s for Honcho)
+while it waits for a read-ahead. Set `gateway.restart_agent_cleanup_seconds`
+(for example `5`) to release them together within that bound on a restart.
+
